{
  "schema": "loom.runtime_profile/1",
  "domain": "chat_coverage",
  "revision": 1,
  "description": "R54 audit as data: everything the user can do must be possible from the conversation window. Every surface of the kernel (a C ABI function, an HTTP route, a loom_invoke operation, a JNI symbol, a settings group or secret) is listed exactly once, as a capability that an action reaches from the conversation (`capabilities`), as something that is not from the chat with a reason (`not_from_chat`), or as a known gap with its plan (`open`). The test tests/test_chat_coverage.cpp fails when the registry (data/graph/interfaces.pack), the settings fields or the loom_invoke dispatcher show a surface that is on none of the three lists, when a list names a surface that is gone, when an action named here is missing, planned or not runnable, and when an example sentence does not reach its action through the router. via: action (an action of the catalogue), client (an action of the catalogue the client carries out itself - one with a `client` member, runnable for a client that declares its capability, e.g. the arrangement of windows), native (the window itself), emergent (offered as a proposal by the growing catalogue). check: route (the examples are routed; the default for actions that have them), phrases (the action carries phrases), continuation (the action is reached from a proposal that another action returns, never from a sentence of its own: it carries no phrases, and the entry says so in chat_outcome_reason). chat_outcome (K2b-2): what the example sentences do when they are sent as chat text - pending (a proposal that waits for the person: the default), unavailable (the proposal says honestly that the sentence alone cannot do it, with the reason in chat_outcome_reason), continuation. An action that runs at once is declared in intent_routing (execution.direct), not here. Everything here is data: an overlay may add entries; nothing is a limit.",
  "defaults": {
    "schema": "loom.chat_coverage/1",
    "sources": {
      "c_abi": "data/graph/interfaces.pack interfaces.c_abi",
      "http": "data/graph/interfaces.pack interfaces.http + interfaces.web (one namespace: \"VERB /path\", parameters as :id)",
      "jni": "data/graph/interfaces.pack interfaces.jni",
      "invoke": "port.operation of loom_invoke, found in src/capi/capi_invoke.cpp, src/actions/runner.cpp (ActionRunner::invoke), src/actions/query.cpp, src/storage/storage_command.cpp and src/capi/capi_media.cpp (github)",
      "settings": "group:<group> of every field of runtime/settings_fields.pack, key:<key> for secrets and internal keys"
    },
    "invoke_ports": {
      "actions": "actions.*",
      "storage": "storage.*",
      "github": "github.*",
      "chat": "chat.*",
      "ports": "ports.*",
      "environments": "environments.*",
      "tool_source": "tool_source.*",
      "agent": "agent.*",
      "memory_folder": "memory.*"
    },
    "capabilities": [
      {
        "id": "chat",
        "title": {
          "en": "Talk to the model",
          "pl": "Rozmowa z modelem"
        },
        "via": "native",
        "surfaces": {
          "c_abi": [
            "loom_chat",
            "loom_chat_ex",
            "loom_chat_cancel"
          ],
          "http": [
            "POST /api/chat",
            "POST /api/chat/cancel",
            "POST /api/chat/route",
            "POST /api/chat/usage-preview",
            "POST /api/graph-reply"
          ],
          "invoke": [
            "chat.route"
          ]
        },
        "note": {
          "en": "The window itself: a message is sent, an answer streams, a command is told apart from a message by the router.",
          "pl": "Samo okienko: wiadomość jest wysyłana, odpowiedź płynie, a polecenie router odróżnia od wiadomości."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "proposal_flow",
        "title": {
          "en": "Answer a proposal: yes, no, cancel",
          "pl": "Odpowiedź na propozycję: tak, nie, anuluj"
        },
        "via": "native",
        "surfaces": {
          "http": [
            "POST /api/actions/run",
            "POST /api/actions/confirm",
            "POST /api/actions/cancel",
            "POST /api/actions/preview",
            "POST /api/actions/client_result"
          ],
          "invoke": [
            "actions.run",
            "actions.confirm",
            "actions.cancel",
            "actions.preview",
            "actions.client_result"
          ]
        },
        "note": {
          "en": "\"yes\" / \"no\" in the conversation (and the buttons of the proposal block) are these calls; a device step is answered by the client.",
          "pl": "„tak” / „nie” w rozmowie (i przyciski bloku propozycji) to te wywołania; krok urządzenia odpowiada klient."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "retrieval",
        "title": {
          "en": "Context the conversation uses on each message",
          "pl": "Kontekst, którego rozmowa używa przy każdej wiadomości"
        },
        "via": "native",
        "surfaces": {
          "c_abi": [
            "loom_select_context",
            "loom_select_context_ex",
            "loom_context_build"
          ],
          "http": [
            "POST /api/context/select",
            "POST /api/context/build"
          ]
        },
        "note": {
          "en": "The retrieval of every message; to look at what is connected, ask for the graph around a name.",
          "pl": "Wyszukiwanie przy każdej wiadomości; żeby zajrzeć w powiązania, poproś o graf wokół nazwy."
        }
      },
      {
